{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/764054-onyx-path-should-take-over-d-d","id":764054,"title":"Onyx Path should take over D&D","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-12T07:57:16-08:00","id":764054,"title":"Onyx Path should take over D&D","content":"I'd like the D&amp;D 5e and forgotten realms to be licienced from WotC/Hasbro to Onyx Path the way CPP and now Paradox? Has done for the World of Darkness and Exalted.<br /> <br /> 5e is a great system and FR and the other settings of D&amp;D are well loved by many, but they seem to beyond WotC's ability to manage right now, and I know many who are happy with lack setting support. D&amp;D is just too understaffed.<br /> <br /> They've already had other publishers do some of thier few products the SCAG, APs, but its been disappointing.<br /> <br /> So why not let Onyx Path run the show, they've already shown they can handle multiple settings, kickstarters, all that stuff.<br /> <br /> There are many experienced freelancers iching to do more D&amp;D work so staff shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> I'm curious as to opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T11:23:56-08:00","id":764230,"title":"","content":"No thanks. I'd rather OP focus their attention of the World of Darkness(both Classic and New). Besides, if I want my fantasy swords and sorcery fix, I have OP's Scarred Lands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T13:00:11-08:00","id":764325,"title":"","content":"How is OP ever supposed to raise the funds to outright buy the D&amp;D IPs from Hasbro/WotC even if it was for sale? <br /> <br /> Even if OP could do a theoretical better job with the IPs than WotC is doing, and not in the process overload themselves, there are so many practical barriers in the way it seems pointless to even consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T15:38:40-08:00","id":764451,"title":"","content":"I'm not at all into the idea of Onyx Path (or anyone else) taking on D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> All of the things I like about 5th edition are things that would invariably be diminished or obliterated by someone else taking over production - including but not limited to being able to pick up releases at my FLGS in hard copy, not missing out on cool stuff because it's locked up in a kickstarter backer reward tier that not only costs more than I want to pay for the nifty this-or-that but also includes stuff that I don't actually want, and that what I like for D&amp;D is not the same as what I like for other games and thus the designers for other games are not the designers I like for D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Plus, the whole reason why this is being brought up - the slow release schedule - is a feature, not a bug. Any faster on the schedule means a drop in playtesting time which means a drop in the quality of the game-stuff, and that's a no-go for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T17:11:17-08:00","id":764536,"title":"","content":"If WotC doesn't have the staff to do D&amp;D, how on earth would we do it? We only have three employees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T20:54:49-08:00","id":764695,"title":"","content":"Let me clarify, I'm not saying OP buys D&amp;D, I doubt Hasbro would sell that, the movie rights are too potentially profitable.<br /> <br /> I'm just talking about setting up a simular arrangement as Onyx Path made with CPP that saved and revived WOD, Exalted, ect...<br /> <br /> As for how would Onyx Path handle D&amp;D, the same way its juggling 2 Vampire Games, 2 Mage Games, 2 Werewolf Games, Changeling the Lost, Promeathan, Beast, Mummy, 2 Demons games, Exalted, Scion, Trinity, Scarred Lands, Pugmere, Cavaliers of Mars.<br /> <br /> Via Kickstarters and Freelancers. There is a large pool of Freelancers with experience in D&amp;D, Onyx Path sets up the kickstarters and hires the freelancers to produce it.<br /> <br /> Its mostly a seperate pool of Freelancers from those they use for WOD so that won't effect the other IPs at all.<br /> <br /> Right now 5e D&amp;D and its settings are not being properly supported by WotC, so I'd rather Onyx Path take over from them on managing D&amp;D and preform the same miracle for Eberron, Forgotten Realms, Darksun, Raven Loft, ect... That they did for WOD, Exalted, Ect...<br /> <br /> Once the ball is rolling maybe hire a couple more full time people at Onyx to help with any extra adminsteration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T21:09:47-08:00","id":764702,"title":"","content":"I have Exalted if I want to run a high fantasy combat engine that occasionally delves into other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T06:22:49-08:00","id":764889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/764054-onyx-path-should-take-over-d-d?p=764695#post764695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now 5e D&amp;D and its settings are not being properly supported by WotC, so I'd rather Onyx Path take over from them on managing D&amp;D and preform the same miracle for Eberron, Forgotten Realms, Darksun, Raven Loft, ect... That they did for WOD, Exalted, Ect....</div> </div> </div> </div>hm....what? They explicitely stated that their release goal was to stop with the monthly 40$ hardcover release with about 10 lines of useful content and 25 useless feats (See D&amp;D 3.5 and 4)<br /> <br /> I am more than happy with the slower D&amp;D release, and I'm glad that OPP has revived Exalted, WoD, Scarred Lands, etc... but I'm looking for a different feel when I play D&amp;D than when I play Scion or Exalted or WoD.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D has clear black and white, flaming magic swords +2, simple D20 rules and our main concern is fighting orcs for loot. I don't want it to become another &quot;everything is gray and you can find allies in the darkest of hearts&quot; - I want to slay that goblin without having a melodramatic scene about how each life matters and thinking that maybe I am the real monster.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: D&amp;D is everything but dead. OPP might not be the best to take care of it. I want my flaming sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T09:29:11-08:00","id":765006,"title":"","content":"Additionally, if Onyx Path published D&amp;D, I'd probably have to buy it. At least the core stuff. And I don't really want to buy D&amp;D. So there's that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T12:31:52-08:00","id":765714,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about releasing $40 books filled with pointless feats and garbage, I'm talking about releasing proper updates of the settings, not goofy filler books.<br /> <br /> And I'm not talking about turning D&amp;D into the World of Dungeons, 5e is a great system, I just want Onyx Path to administer things, hold the kickstarters, hire the free lancers, and let them do it.<br /> <br /> The James Brothers, Ed Greenwood, Elaine Cunningham, Eric Boyd, Erin M. Evans, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T12:35:52-08:00","id":765717,"title":"","content":"5E was a return to every old problem of DnD before 4E with some more problems thrown in.<br /> <br /> Like, love or hate 4E, you have to admit it was trying to do something different then keep making the same kinds of mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T12:36:29-08:00","id":765718,"title":"","content":"Why would you be required to buy D&amp;D core books for 5e if Onyx Path took over?<br /> <br /> Aside from the fact that the 5e Core books already exist, so Onyx Path would be doing them in the first place.<br /> <br /> White Wolf back in the day published the Raven Loft D&amp;D setting and Onyx Paths roots are in WW, so in a sense its not without presedence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T13:09:37-08:00","id":765741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/764054-onyx-path-should-take-over-d-d?p=765718#post765718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf back in the day published the Raven Loft D&amp;D setting and Onyx Paths roots are in WW, so in a sense its not without presedence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahha, I just thinked about writing this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm recently eating myself through the 3rd ed Ravenloft books, well, because I like 5e and want to DMing/play RL. They are very good IMO. Since WoTC is not seems to making any other settings in the near future, is it too unrealistic from OP to approach WoTC and offer to 3rd partying RL to them? WoTC already outsourced every books over the cores, so it would be potentionaly a win-win situation to everyone, wouldn't it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 11-14-2015, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T17:54:32-08:00","id":765920,"title":"","content":"I honestly wouldn't mind seeing WotC license Eberron out to Onyx Path. I'd even give 5e a shot if they did that, although I'd prefer if it stayed with d20/PFRPG as its system. <br /> <br /> If they were ever to do the same thing with Planescape, I'd go totally nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T20:29:20-08:00","id":766024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/764054-onyx-path-should-take-over-d-d?p=765717#post765717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5E was a return to every old problem of DnD before 4E with some more problems thrown in.<br /> <br /> Like, love or hate 4E, you have to admit it was trying to do something different then keep making the same kinds of mistakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>4E remains the best edition of DnD simply because it was honest about itself. DnD is, and has always been, a tactical simulator. It came out of Chainmail and never moved more than half a step away. It remains extremely puzzling to me why DnD fans would prefer their tactical simulator buried under tons of broken unwieldy mechanics that exist for no other reason than to make you pretend you are not actually playing a tactical simulator.<br /> <br /> 4E had some huge issues, mind you. Still the best DnD so far, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T20:36:42-08:00","id":766026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/764054-onyx-path-should-take-over-d-d?p=766024#post766024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4E remains the best edition of DnD simply because it was honest about itself. DnD is, and has always been, a tactical simulator. It came out of Chainmail and never moved more than half a step away. It remains extremely puzzling to me why DnD fans would prefer their tactical simulator buried under tons of broken unwieldy mechanics that exist for no other reason than to make you pretend you are not actually playing a tactical simulator.<br /> <br /> 4E had some huge issues, mind you. Still the best DnD so far, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who almost solely plays Planescape, I must disagree. D&amp;D is at its heart a tactical simulator, yes. It is far from just that though. 4e was a perfectly feasible game. If they had marketed it a Magic: The Gathering RPG, I think it would would have been a home run. <br /> <br /> It was never really D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T08:49:22-08:00","id":766288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/764054-onyx-path-should-take-over-d-d?p=766024#post766024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It remains extremely puzzling to me why DnD fans would prefer their tactical simulator buried under tons of broken unwieldy mechanics that exist for no other reason than to make you pretend you are not actually playing a tactical simulator.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's one opinion. I agree, that the previous editions were very... combat oriented to put it diplomaticly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> However, 5e did a lot of step toward more narrative-orientedness both in the rules and in tone and this was actualy bringing me back to DnD. The combat chapter in the PHB is 10 pages and the whole combat grid thing is absolutely optional. That is exactly why I think it would be cool if OP would make Ravenlof material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T13:57:44-08:00","id":766511,"title":"","content":"I don't really agree that combat focus of DnD is a problem. It's what the game is about. The entire premise of the game is that you get to pick a hero, and classes represent various ways to kill a monster in an empty rectangular room. In all editions, it's a game where you advance by killing stuff. A character who has no way of killing stuff is worse than useless at a DnD table, not to mention very unlikely to create as there are no meaningful stats besides ones that describe how well you kill stuff.<br /> <br /> Now, all I know about 5E is what I read during beta - I haven't read it as published (though apparently I will as my wife expressed annoyance at being apparently the only role player alive without any DnD experience). But I have trouble believing that it suddenly became a narrative-oriented game. The narrative serves only to provide a reason to find yourself in a rectangular room and kill a monster. Which is fine! Let's just accept that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T14:07:31-08:00","id":766521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/764054-onyx-path-should-take-over-d-d?p=766511#post766511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really agree that combat focus of DnD is a problem. It's what the game is about. The entire premise of the game is that you get to pick a hero, and classes represent various ways to kill a monster in an empty rectangular room. In all editions, it's a game where you advance by killing stuff. A character who has no way of killing stuff is worse than useless at a DnD table, not to mention very unlikely to create as there are no meaningful stats besides ones that describe how well you kill stuff.<br /> <br /> Now, all I know about 5E is what I read during beta - I haven't read it as published (though apparently I will as my wife expressed annoyance at being apparently the only role player alive without any DnD experience). But I have trouble believing that it suddenly became a narrative-oriented game. The narrative serves only to provide a reason to find yourself in a rectangular room and kill a monster. Which is fine! Let's just accept that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is absolutely not true. It may be true of what you have played, but the narrative is not just an excuse to get to combat. If it was, Eberron and Planescape would never have existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T14:33:50-08:00","id":766542,"title":"","content":"Never played Eberron though I know the premise, but I did play Planescape. It was a very interesting experience and an absolutely positive one. But you don't have to go there, Ravenloft, Dragonlance, Dark Sun... pretty much every D&amp;D setting has a strong and interesting narrative behind it. Behind being the key word. I just don't think the game mechanically engages any of it. To this day I'm sad Planescape had no mechanical support for awesome ideas it contained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T16:34:02-08:00","id":766633,"title":"","content":"A slight factual nitpick on that:<br /> <br /> Early D&amp;D was not about killing everything. It was about how much loot you could get out of with. It often made combat a suboptimal choice compared to stealth if possible.<br /> <br /> Though that doesn't mean any edition actually mechanically supported a lot of the settings provided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T07:17:07-08:00","id":767047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dawngreeter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/764054-onyx-path-should-take-over-d-d?p=766024#post766024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4E remains the best edition of DnD simply because it was honest about itself. DnD is, and has always been, a tactical simulator. It came out of Chainmail and never moved more than half a step away. It remains extremely puzzling to me why DnD fans would prefer their tactical simulator buried under tons of broken unwieldy mechanics that exist for no other reason than to make you pretend you are not actually playing a tactical simulator.<br /> <br /> 4E had some huge issues, mind you. Still the best DnD so far, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T09:26:39-08:00","id":767120,"title":"","content":"5e has a big thing with what they call the 3 pillars: combat, exploration, and interaction. It is kind of expected that all player characters will participate in each to some degree. It's definitely not a narratively focused game, but it's not a tactical combat simulator either. In fact, for the design of the combat rules in this edition they prioritized ease of use and speed of resolution over tactics and simulation, much to the dismay of many 4e fans and the joy of many OSR fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T12:48:26-08:00","id":767229,"title":"","content":"...Is that Jessica Rabbit taking a selfie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T15:13:02-08:00","id":767371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/764054-onyx-path-should-take-over-d-d?p=767229#post767229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Is that Jessica Rabbit taking a selfie?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Looker from The Outsiders. It's hard to see at the size it displays here, but she doesn't actually show up on the camera screen (being a vampire and all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","us